# Anchoring convention
#
# `.gitattributes` patterns anchor the same way `.gitignore` patterns do, so the convention
# documented at the top of `.gitignore` applies here too: a slash anywhere but the end anchors the
# pattern to this file's directory, so declare the intent on every pattern containing a slash.

# Visual regression baselines. Git cannot delta PNGs, so without LFS every change that touches
# every baseline would add another full set to the pack, permanently, for every clone. A token
# rename does that.
#
# `filter.lfs.required` is deliberately not set here or anywhere in tracked config: it is the only
# key that makes `git add` fail rather than silently commit the raw PNG, but it gates reads too, so
# on a machine with no `git-lfs` binary it makes `git status` and `git switch` fatal on an
# unmodified tree. The Yarn plugin at `.yarn/plugins/plugin-git-lfs.cjs` sets it per-clone, once
# the binary is known to be present, and `lint-staged` plus CI catch a raw PNG either way.
**/__screenshots__/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
